comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-09T21:40:16.394Z","harness:codex","Implement alongside pm-ik19 in one reviewed lifecycle tranche. Preserve historical SDK action identities and output envelopes while making canonical claim/release/close compositions directly discoverable. Start with failing sandbox parity tests, then shared SDK behavior and CLI/MCP contracts."
  "2026-09-09T21:58:48.944Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: shared SDK lifecycle compositions now own claim/start, open/release and close/release sequences. CLI handlers and MCP dispatch call the same functions. Public convenience methods infer compound return envelopes for literal composition flags and preserve base result types otherwise. Focused SDK/CLI suites passed seven tests including flat transport controls, real stored closure evidence and rejected incompatible selection. Broader gates remain pending."
  "2026-09-09T22:04:53.495Z","harness:codex","Verification: typecheck passed. Focused lifecycle, bulk rollback, Bash completion, grammar and completion suites passed 138 tests. SDK snapshot reviewed: additive opt-in conditional return signatures preserve base receipts without composition flags; schema literal versions advance for the new boolean controls. Full coverage and static gates are still running."
  "2026-09-09T22:19:40.547Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: packaged CLI installed and passed isolated create, claim --start, release --pause, update many, close --release-assignment, close delete dry-run and strict history verification with npm and Bun. Docs/skills full gate and unchanged flag/help-token budget gate now pass. Full-suite run exposed stale test expectations and concurrent-build imports; those are being resolved before a stable full coverage rerun."
  "2026-09-09T22:23:51.080Z","harness:codex","Regression evidence: shared composition retains MCP literal-input provenance through every option copy. The canonical literal-dash test and existing open-stdin MCP handshake regression now pass; focused final run passed all 66 tests across MCP, SDK composition, item addressing and namespace completion."
  "2026-09-09T22:32:10.352Z","harness:codex","Validation evidence: packed npx and bunx smoke passed version 2026.9.9 with all 13 packages and a plain TypeScript SDK consumer. Typechecks passed. Static assurance retains 100 percent docstrings. Grammar gate exposed omitted deprecated task aliases in discovery; fixing the gate to independently load their live help, with positive and missing-registration tests, preserving compact discovery and fail-closed behavior. Full coverage remains running."
  "2026-09-09T22:45:51.649Z","harness:codex","Verification update: all three linked test commands passed. The full 657-file run reached 8653 passes and one stale next-step assertion; that assertion now expects canonical claim --start and full coverage is rerunning with failure reports enabled. ESLint, duplicate checks, static assurance, 57-surface byte ratchet, context evaluation, compatibility against published 2026.9.9, 88-command package dogfood, and required Sentry/telemetry aggregate health passed. Isolated import-cost verification and final exact coverage remain pending."
  "2026-09-09T23:01:34.459Z","harness:codex","Final local verification: 657 test files and all 8656 tests passed. Exact all-source coverage is statements 63848/63848, branches 48570/48570, functions 13265/13265, lines 61217/61217: 100/100/100/100 with no exclusions or lowered thresholds introduced. Source CLI integration now executes real canonical and alias handlers under coverage while packed npm/Bun acceptance remains independent. Quiet SDK import-cost gate passed 10 entrypoints and CLI transport-floor gate passed 6 operations. All previously recorded local quality gates and 100 percent docstrings remain passing. Implementation is ready for reviewed delivery; hosted PR and merge evidence is still pending."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-09T22:43:37.133Z","harness:codex","Architecture: sdk/lifecycle/task-composition owns start, pause and close/release sequencing. CLI and MCP dispatch share those functions; PmClient and convenience functions infer full compound receipt types for literal true controls. These are ordered compositions, not cross-operation transactions; partial success remains inspectable through constituent history. Broad MCP start remains scheduling text, while action-specific claim discovery types start as boolean and options carries it through broad tools."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-09T22:38:28.893Z","harness:codex","Preserve mutation transport provenance when composing SDK operations: use mutationOptionsWithOverrides so MCP literal dashes do not become stdin reads. Keep exhaustive live grammar verification independent of compact discovery by probing hidden aliases through registered help."
